<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Howden year share rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Howden year share rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended April 30, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		40.0	   vs 38.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 12.0	   vs n/a</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   24.3	   vs 19.6</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   40.9	   vs 30.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 13.3	   vs 9.1</p>
<p>Net financial revenue 1.9 received vs 1.6 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  404.8	  vs 295.5</p>
<p>Div payable September 30</p>
<p>on register September 5</p>
<p>Full name: Howden Africa Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Reporting maiden full year results, directors said that the outlook for the markets which Howden serves, which includes power generation, mining, agriculture, construction and steel, looked good.</p>
<p>Exports through emerging markets in South America, Pacific Basin, the United Arab Emirates and the rest of Africa were expected to grow.</p>
<p>As a result of the takeover of international engineering group Charter Plc, Howden's year end will change to December 1997 and the group will report results for the eight-month period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
